# Grainlet auth-sdk (`grainlet/auth-sdk`)

Use when you need browser SDK loading / popups. Wire tokens into `grainlet/auth` providers. Prefer custom `authorize` if your API is not the SDK defaults.

```js
import {
  createAuthSdk, AuthSdkError, loadScript,
  getGoogleIdToken, GoogleSignIn,
  getAppleCredential, AppleSignIn,
  getGitHubAuthorization, completeGitHubSignIn, GitHubSignIn,
  GITHUB_CALLBACK_MESSAGE,
  createOAuthState, openCenteredPopup, waitForPopupMessage,
} from 'grainlet/auth-sdk';
```

```js
// Full SDK (expects backend routes matching auth-sdk defaults)
const sdk = createAuthSdk({ google: { clientId }, apple: { clientId }, github: { clientId } });
await sdk.signInWithGoogle(); // posts to default /api/auth/google unless customized

// Google — custom backend (recommended when API differs)
const idToken = await getGoogleIdToken({ clientId: GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID });
// or: await GoogleSignIn({ clientId }) → { idToken, ... }

// Apple
const apple = await getAppleCredential({ clientId, redirectURI });
// or: await AppleSignIn({ clientId, redirectURI })

// GitHub popup flow
const { code, state } = await getGitHubAuthorization({ clientId });
await completeGitHubSignIn({ code, state }); // or GitHubSignIn({ clientId })
// popup page posts: { type: GITHUB_CALLBACK_MESSAGE, ... }
```

```js
await loadScript('https://accounts.google.com/gsi/client');
const state = createOAuthState();
const popup = openCenteredPopup(url, 'oauth');
const message = await waitForPopupMessage(popup, { type: GITHUB_CALLBACK_MESSAGE });

try {
  await getGoogleIdToken({ clientId });
} catch (e) {
  if (e instanceof AuthSdkError) console.error(e.code);
}
```

```js
// Bad — createAuthSdk when backend body/path is custom (e.g. /api/auth/sync)
await createAuthSdk({ google: { clientId } }).signInWithGoogle();
// Good — getGoogleIdToken + Google({ getIdToken, authorize }) in grainlet/auth
```
